DEGREES OF FREEDOM\par
Definition: The number of independent parameters that define the configuration of a mechanical system. In robotics, it typically refers to the number of independent movements a robot's joints can make.\par
Function: Determines the robot's dexterity and ability to reach different positions and orientations in its workspace. A higher number of degrees of freedom generally allows for more complex movements and tasks.\par
Portuguese Translation: Graus de Liberdade\par

