\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
LADDER LOGIC\par
Definition: A programming language used to program a PLC, graphically representing a program by a diagram based on the circuit diagrams of relay logic hardware.\par
Function: To provide a visual and intuitive way to program industrial control systems, mimicking electrical relay circuits. It's widely used for its ease of understanding and troubleshooting by electricians and control engineers.\par
Portuguese Translation: L\'f3gica Ladder (ou Diagrama Ladder)\par
HMI\par
Definition: (Human-Machine Interface) A user interface or dashboard that connects a person to a machine, system, or device. It provides a graphical representation of the control system and allows operators to monitor and control processes.\par
Function: To facilitate interaction between human operators and automated systems, providing real-time data, alarms, and control capabilities. HMIs are crucial for monitoring performance, troubleshooting issues, and making adjustments in industrial and process control environments.\par
Portuguese Translation: IHM (Interface Homem-M\'e1quina)\par

