\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
OPEN LOOP\par
Definition: A control system in which the control action is independent of the output. There is no feedback mechanism to compare the actual output with the desired output.\par
Function: To execute a predetermined control action without monitoring the result. It is simpler and less expensive to implement but less accurate and cannot compensate for disturbances or errors.\par
Portuguese Translation: Malha Aberta\par
CLOSED LOOP\par
Definition: A control system in which the control action is dependent on the output. It uses feedback to compare the actual output with the desired output and adjusts the control action accordingly.\par
Function: To achieve and maintain a desired output by continuously monitoring the system's performance and making corrections. It is more accurate and robust than open-loop control, capable of compensating for disturbances and errors.\par
Portuguese Translation: Malha Fechada\par

