SENSOR\par
Definition: A device that detects and responds to some type of input from the physical environment. The input could be light, heat, motion, moisture, pressure, or any one of a great number of other environmental phenomena.\par
Function: To convert physical parameters into electrical signals that can be measured, interpreted, and used by control systems. Sensors provide the necessary data for automated systems to understand their environment and make informed decisions.\par
