\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
ACTUATOR\par
Definition: A component of a machine that is responsible for moving and controlling a mechanism or system, for example, by opening a valve, turning on a pump, or moving a robotic arm. It takes energy, usually created by air, electric current, or liquid, and converts that into some kind of motion.\par
Function: To convert a control signal (electrical, pneumatic, or hydraulic) into physical motion or action. Actuators are the 'muscles' of an automated system, executing the commands issued by controllers based on sensor input.\par
Portuguese Translation: Atuador\par

