SERVO MOTOR\par
Definition: A rotary or linear actuator that allows for precise control of angular or linear position, velocity, and acceleration. It consists of a motor, a feedback device (like an encoder), and a control circuit.\par
Function: To provide precise motion control in applications requiring high accuracy and repeatability, such as robotics, CNC machinery, and automated manufacturing. The feedback mechanism allows the servo motor to maintain its commanded position or speed.\par
Portuguese Translation: Servo Motor\par

