TRANSDUCER\par
Definition: A device that converts energy from one form to another. This conversion can be from a physical quantity (like pressure, temperature, or light) into an electrical signal, or vice versa.\par
Function: To enable communication between different types of systems or to measure physical phenomena. Sensors are a type of transducer that convert physical energy into electrical signals, while actuators are transducers that convert electrical signals into physical motion.\par
Portuguese Translation: Transdutor\par

